CanonicalLibraryNode B, explicit actual vectorL2 prerequisite (not a covariance certificate):

theorem gibbs_linear_covariance_upper
    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] [CompleteSpace E]
    (W : E → ℝ) (hW : ContDiff ℝ 2 W)
    (hI : Integrable (fun x => Real.exp (-W x)))
    (hZ : 0 < ∫ x, Real.exp (-W x))
    (m M : ℝ) (hm : 0 < m) (hmM : m ≤ M)
    (hlower : ∀ x a, m*‖a‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ W) x a a)
    (hupper : ∀ x a, fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ W) x a a ≤ M*‖a‖^2)
    (hX : MemLp id 2 ((volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -W x))) :
    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -W x)
    ∀ a : E, ProbabilityTheory.covarianceBilin μ a a ≤ ‖a‖^2/m

SourceAnchor A, source beta=1 and alpha=kappa^-1, eta cap retained:

theorem smoothed_hessian_bounds
    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] [CompleteSpace E]
    {V : E → ℝ} {κ η : ℝ}
    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)
    (hH : ∀ x a : E, κ⁻¹*‖a‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x a a ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x a a ≤ ‖a‖^2)
    (hη : 0 < η) (hη1 : η ≤ 1) :
    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)
    let C := ((Real.sqrt (2*Real.pi*η))⁻¹)^Module.finrank ℝ E
    let A := fun y : E => C*∫ x, Real.exp (-V x-‖y-x‖^2/(2*η)) ∂(volume : Measure E)
    let Vη := fun y => -Real.log (A y)
    let R := fun y : E => μ.tilted (fun x => -‖x-y‖^2/(2*η))
    IsProbabilityMeasure μ ∧ ContDiff ℝ 2 Vη ∧
      (∀ y, IsProbabilityMeasure (R y) ∧ MemLp id 2 (R y) ∧
        (∀ a, ProbabilityTheory.covarianceBilin (R y) a a ≤ ‖a‖^2/(κ⁻¹+η⁻¹)) ∧
        ∀ a, (1/(κ+η))*‖a‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ Vη) y a a ∧
          fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ Vη) y a a ≤ (1/(1+η))*‖a‖^2) ∧
      LipschitzWith (1 : ℝ≥0) (gradient Vη)

The B moment condition is genuine integrability required to connect totalized covarianceBilin to actual covariance; the A statement has no moment premise and must derive posterior vectorL2. Canonical B retains BOTH curvature and actual partition. Source A retains its source cap and normalization. Finite Hilbert/Borel including0 is a disclosed representation extension of source Euclidean space, not a nontrivial-space assumption. No anisotropic BL, reflected quarter law, Markov selector, algorithm/main/Wp/initialization/cost/composition is admitted by this proposal. The actual source U=Veta+logZ adapter is an internal proof obligation.
